== 6. Pooled Spearman, core vs shore vs distal =================
  shore and distal are pre-specified controls: the core should be the
  strongest and most negative if the association is promoter-specific.

  RASSF9:
    set           n      rho           p
    core        741   -0.383    2.34e-27
    shore       741    0.520    1.37e-52
    distal      741    0.291    6.86e-16
    detection ~ core: OR per 0.1 beta = 0.463, p = 9.01e-14 (n = 741, 19.6% detected)

  RASSF10:
    set           n      rho           p
    core        741   -0.562    5.44e-63
    shore       741   -0.418    1.22e-32
    distal      741    0.157    1.76e-05
    detection ~ core: OR per 0.1 beta = 0.626, p = 6.88e-18 (n = 741, 24.2% detected)


== 7. Nested adjustment ========================================
  Reported as in scripts 36 and 40: beta, CI, and percentage of the
  unadjusted effect retained. Lineage is the critical covariate -- if the
  effect vanishes with lineage in the model, it is composition.

  RASSF9  (n = 736 lines, 23 lineages):
    M0 unadjusted            n =  736  beta = -1.384 [-1.642, -1.127]  p = 2.56e-24   100% retained
    M1 + lineage             n =  736  beta = -1.160 [-1.438, -0.881]  p = 1.56e-15    84% retained
    M2 + log2 CN             n =  611  beta = -1.456 [-1.749, -1.164]  p = 5.19e-21   105% retained
    M3 + lineage + log2 CN   n =  611  beta = -1.234 [-1.551, -0.917]  p = 9.91e-14    89% retained
    premise: CN vs expression   rho = +0.138, p = 0.00062
    premise: CN vs core beta    rho = +0.005, p = 0.91
    A covariate unrelated to both cannot be confounding the result.

  RASSF10  (n = 736 lines, 23 lineages):
    M0 unadjusted            n =  736  beta = -1.485 [-1.723, -1.247]  p = 1.96e-31   100% retained
    M1 + lineage             n =  736  beta = -1.302 [-1.555, -1.048]  p = 2.47e-22    88% retained
    M2 + log2 CN             n =  611  beta = -1.368 [-1.631, -1.105]  p = 1.23e-22    92% retained
    M3 + lineage + log2 CN   n =  611  beta = -1.278 [-1.556, -1.000]  p = 2.71e-18    86% retained
    premise: CN vs expression   rho = +0.241, p = 1.66e-09
    premise: CN vs core beta    rho = -0.135, p = 0.000826
    A covariate unrelated to both cannot be confounding the result.

