== 11. Limits to carry into the write-up =======================
  1. This is a PAN-CANCER analysis. It does not establish a
     methylation-expression relationship WITHIN melanoma cells, which
     remains untestable because expression there has no variance.
  2. A SUPPORTED verdict means methylation tracks expression across
     cancer cells, with melanoma at the methylated-and-silent end. It
     does not show methylation CAUSED the silencing. Demethylation in
     vitro is the experiment that would.
  3. A COMPOSITION verdict means the pooled correlation reflects lineages
     differing in both variables. That is still informative -- it is how
     a lineage-restricted epigenetic state looks -- but it is a weaker
     claim and must be labelled as such.
  4. Methylation (Sanger) and expression and copy number (Broad) come
     from different laboratories and different cell stocks.
  5. Cell lines are not tumours.
